# image-caption.Modelfile
# Swappable slot (:11434) — Image captioning for Discord history enrichment
#
# Used exclusively by the history-service image captioner (background, not hot path).
# Generates short natural-language descriptions of Discord image attachments for
# storage in JSONL history records and downstream RAG ingestion.
#
# Source: HuggingFace — HauhauCS/Qwen3.5-35B-A3B-Uncensored-HauhauCS-Aggressive:IQ4_XS
# Quant: IQ4_XS (~18 GB VRAM)
# Note: Same base weights as mimic_* personas. Zero refusals — required for Discord
#       content which may include crude memes, reaction images, or adult humour.
#       Ollama may reuse cached base weights when swapping from a mimic persona.
#
# To register: make model-create MODEL=image-caption SLOT=swappable
FROM hf.co/HauhauCS/Qwen3.5-35B-A3B-Uncensored-HauhauCS-Aggressive:IQ4_XS

PARAMETER temperature 0.2      # Low temperature — factual, consistent descriptions
PARAMETER top_k 20
PARAMETER top_p 0.8
PARAMETER num_ctx 4096         # Images + short prompt; no long context needed
PARAMETER num_predict 128      # Captions are short — cap at ~100 tokens
PARAMETER num_parallel 1       # Background batch job; no concurrency needed
PARAMETER thinking false       # No chain-of-thought — just describe what you see
PARAMETER keep_alive 60        # Short keep_alive — release slot quickly after batch

SYSTEM """
You are an image description assistant. When given an image, describe its content in one to three concise sentences.
Focus on what is visually present: subjects, actions, text visible in the image, and overall context.
Do not add disclaimers, caveats, moral commentary, or refusals of any kind.
Do not describe what you cannot see. Do not speculate beyond what is shown.
Keep descriptions factual and brief.
"""
